{
  "id": "contexts/switching/01_two_hosts",
  "topic": "contexts",
  "subtopic": "switching",
  "title": "Choosing a header's host",
  "summary": "A header that relies on its includer reads the way the chosen includer makes it",
  "prose": "`shared.h` uses a macro that each source defines before including it. Both sources are contexts of the header: clice picks one, the editor can switch to the other, and hover then shows the type that host gives. The choice is kept across restarts until it is reset.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "int_host.cpp",
      "text": "#define VALUE_TYPE int\n#include \"shared.h\"\n\nint main() {\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "real_host.cpp",
      "text": "#define VALUE_TYPE float\n#include \"shared.h\"\n\nfloat real() {\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "shared.h",
      "text": "#pragma once\n\nVALUE_TYPE get_value();\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
